# README.md is prettier-ignored here as it already is in the typescript and js clients.
# .prettierrc sets useTabs, so prettier re-tabs the fenced code blocks that markdownlint's
# MD010 then de-tabs, and .husky/pre-commit runs `make prettier -w` before `pre-commit run`
# -- so the two fight on every commit that touches the file and none of them can ever pass.
# Prettier also rewrites the `[comment]: <> (START/END OF GITHUB README)` slice markers the
# release Makefile cuts the published README with.
